# --- Generated by the cube pipeline (`npm run cube` in web/) -------------------
# Card images (~16 MB) and cube JSON are rebuilt from cubes/sources.json +
# cubes/*.txt by the pipeline; any build/deploy step must run `npm run cube`
# first. The cubes/*.txt caches ARE tracked: they are the fallback when
# Moxfield is unreachable.
web/public/cards/
web/public/cubes/

# Placeholder icons are generated by `npm run icons` (web/scripts/make-icons.mjs)
web/public/icons/

# --- Dependencies and build output ----------------------------------------------
node_modules/
# One project, three build channels (APP-MIGRATION.md section 3).
dist/
web/dist-app/
web/dist-imsg/

# --- Planning documents (kept locally, not part of the repository) -------------
DESIGN.md
APP-MIGRATION.md

# --- Local tooling / session state ---------------------------------------------
.claude/
.agents/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# --- OS / editor noise ----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
/design

# --- Generated by the banlist / catalogue / lookup pipelines -------------------
# Rebuilt by `npm run generate` (wired into prebuild, so any `npm run build`
# regenerates them). The SOURCES are tracked instead: lookup/land-cycles.json is
# hand-authored, and banlists/3cb-official.json is the scrape cache -- the
# fallback when 3cardblind.com is unreachable, and the only record of what the
# list said on a given date, since that site has no API and no version history.
# The catalogue is 2.4 MB of Scryfall bulk data that changes daily; committing
# it would add that much binary to history on every refresh.
web/public/catalogue/
web/public/banlist/
web/public/lookup/
